            <ArticleTitle>Off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting in patients with mirror-imaging dextrocardia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>643-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocs.12582</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dextrocardia requires alterations in techniques during coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) surgery. We report two cases undergoing off-pump coronary artery bypass graft (OPCAB) surgery and discuss techniques for the operative management of these patients.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2015 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
